    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6u3k0px",
      "content": "Sociology is the scientific study of society, social relationships, institutions, and human behavior within social groups. In nursing, sociology helps nurses understand the social factors that influence health, illness, health behavior, and healthcare utilization. Social determinants such as family structure, culture, education, income, and environment significantly affect patient health outcomes. In nursing competitive examinations such as RRB Nursing, common questions are asked from social structure, social institutions, culture, family, socialization, social problems, and health-related sociological concepts."
    },
    {
      "id": "pw095mf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Basic Sociological Concepts"
    },
    {
      "id": "gwfgjoe",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Society</p>",
            "<p>A group of people living together in an organized community with shared culture and institutions</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Social Interaction</p>",
            "<p>Process by which people act and react in relation to others</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Social Structure</p>",
            "<p>Organized pattern of relationships and institutions that form society</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Social System</p>",
            "<p>Network of relationships forming a coherent whole</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Community</p>",
            "<p>Group of individuals living in a defined geographic area sharing common interests</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
